1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,699
Who can create, edit, publish, or delete a content item?

2
00:00:04,699 --> 00:00:07,324
Orchard Core answers with permissions.

3
00:00:07,324 --> 00:00:11,380
In this video, you allow a role to work with one content type,

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:14,900
and you see how ownership changes what a user can do.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,068
Content permissions come in two levels.

6
00:00:22,068 --> 00:00:25,435
The Contents permissions apply to every content type.

7
00:00:25,435 --> 00:00:29,772
The permissions of one content type apply to that type only, and exist

8
00:00:29,772 --> 00:00:32,340
only when the type is marked Securable.

9
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:39,499
For a securable type, you can allow viewing, previewing, editing, cloning, publishing, deleting,

10
00:00:39,499 --> 00:00:41,259
and listing its items.

11
00:00:41,259 --> 00:00:45,280
A separate permission covers editing the owner of an item.

12
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:48,350
Most actions come in two forms:

13
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:52,677
one for items you own, and one for items that belong to others.

14
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:58,697
Edit Article covers your own articles, and Edit Article for others covers everyone else's.

15
00:00:58,697 --> 00:01:01,770
The owner is the user who created the item.

16
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,597
A higher permission includes the lower ones.

17
00:01:05,597 --> 00:01:10,952
The Contents permission Edit content for others includes Edit Article for others.

18
00:01:10,952 --> 00:01:16,060
Publish includes edit, and edit for others includes view, preview, and clone.

19
00:01:20,265 --> 00:01:24,674
Permissions for a single type appear only when the type is Securable.

20
00:01:24,674 --> 00:01:28,496
The Content Types page is under Design, Content Definition.

21
00:01:28,496 --> 00:01:29,965
Let's find Article.

22
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:31,601
We open Article.

23
00:01:31,601 --> 00:01:36,555
Among its settings, Securable determines whether the type can have custom permissions.

24
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:39,516
It is not checked for Article, so let's check it.

25
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,125
We save the type.

26
00:01:41,125 --> 00:01:44,790
Types you create with Create new type are securable from the start.

27
00:01:48,929 --> 00:01:51,017
Permissions are granted to roles.

28
00:01:51,017 --> 00:01:55,141
Under Access Control, Roles, let's choose Add Role to create a role for

29
00:01:55,141 --> 00:01:57,069
the people who write articles.

30
00:01:57,605 --> 00:02:02,318
We name the role Writer, add a description, and choose Save & Configure.

31
00:02:02,318 --> 00:02:04,735
The role's permissions page opens.

32
00:02:06,619 --> 00:02:09,068
Every permission has two checkboxes.

33
00:02:09,068 --> 00:02:11,925
Allow is a permission you grant explicitly.

34
00:02:11,925 --> 00:02:17,639
Effective is what the role gets in the end, including permissions that a higher one implies.

35
00:02:18,112 --> 00:02:21,605
Users need Access admin panel to use the admin at all.

36
00:02:21,605 --> 00:02:24,282
We search for admin panel, and allow it.

37
00:02:24,737 --> 00:02:26,689
Next, we search for Article.

38
00:02:26,689 --> 00:02:31,568
Its permissions have their own group, Article Content Type - Article, and every

39
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:33,117
label names the type.

40
00:02:33,587 --> 00:02:38,519
We allow Publish or unpublish Article, which applies to articles the user owns,

41
00:02:38,519 --> 00:02:42,464
and List Article content items, so the role can open the list.

42
00:02:42,464 --> 00:02:44,727
The for others versions stay off.

43
00:02:45,193 --> 00:02:49,633
We open the menu beside Save and choose the entry labeled and continue,

44
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:51,940
which saves and stays on the role.

45
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:55,054
The Effective column shows more than we allowed:

46
00:02:55,054 --> 00:02:58,803
Edit Article is ticked, because publishing implies editing.

47
00:02:59,263 --> 00:03:02,436
Hovering over an Effective checkbox explains it.

48
00:03:02,436 --> 00:03:06,080
Edit Article is implied by Publish or unpublish Article.

49
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:10,663
View Article by others comes from the Anonymous and Authenticated roles.

50
00:03:14,871 --> 00:03:17,215
Many roles hold Contents permissions.

51
00:03:17,215 --> 00:03:20,321
Let's open the Editor role, and search for Article.

52
00:03:20,777 --> 00:03:27,089
In the Article group, nothing is allowed explicitly, but the Effective column is ticked almost everywhere.

53
00:03:27,089 --> 00:03:30,977
The Editor role gets those permissions from the Contents group.

54
00:03:31,458 --> 00:03:35,332
Searching for content for others shows the Contents permissions.

55
00:03:35,332 --> 00:03:40,035
Editor is allowed Edit content for others, and that permission applies to every

56
00:03:40,035 --> 00:03:42,138
content type, including Article.

57
00:03:46,362 --> 00:03:49,977
This is the list of articles as Jamie sees it, a user who

58
00:03:49,977 --> 00:03:51,813
was given the Writer role.

59
00:03:51,813 --> 00:03:58,182
The New Article button is there because creating an article needs Edit Article, which publishing implies.

60
00:03:58,182 --> 00:04:01,222
The list also holds articles by the admin user.

61
00:04:01,694 --> 00:04:05,901
Jamie chooses New Article, enters a title, and publishes.

62
00:04:05,901 --> 00:04:11,844
The Publish button is there because the role allows publishing articles Jamie owns.

63
00:04:12,312 --> 00:04:17,200
Back in the list, Team Offsite Notes has a linked title and an Edit button.

64
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:22,872
Jamie owns this article, so the Edit Article permission, implied by publishing, applies.

65
00:04:23,329 --> 00:04:26,087
About and Press Kit belong to the admin user.

66
00:04:26,087 --> 00:04:30,089
Their titles are plain text and there is no Edit button, because the

67
00:04:30,089 --> 00:04:32,739
role does not have Edit Article for others.

68
00:04:33,238 --> 00:04:37,130
Jamie can see the articles of the admin user as well, because the

69
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:40,529
Anonymous and Authenticated roles hold View all content.

70
00:04:40,529 --> 00:04:44,038
Seeing an article and editing it are separate permissions.

71
00:04:48,238 --> 00:04:52,758
To let the role edit every article, allow Edit Article for others.

72
00:04:52,758 --> 00:04:58,848
To cover every content type, allow the Contents permission Edit content for others instead.

73
00:04:59,598 --> 00:05:01,684
Permissions only add access.

74
00:05:01,684 --> 00:05:08,064
A user gets everything that any of their roles allows, plus what Anonymous and Authenticated hold.

75
00:05:08,064 --> 00:05:11,378
No role removes access that another role grants.

76
00:05:12,128 --> 00:05:16,878
Anonymous holds View all content by default, so every visitor can read the

77
00:05:16,878 --> 00:05:19,016
published items of every type.

78
00:05:19,016 --> 00:05:22,164
Taking that permission away affects every type.

79
00:05:22,164 --> 00:05:25,668
A separate video covers building a members-only area.

80
00:05:27,668 --> 00:05:29,536
That's content permissions:

81
00:05:29,536 --> 00:05:33,557
grant them for all content or for one securable type, for items a

82
00:05:33,557 --> 00:05:36,445
user owns or for items that belong to others.

83
00:05:36,445 --> 00:05:37,918
Thanks for watching.

